From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:21:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] drm/i915/dp: the HD audio of a converter whose display
 data declare stereo only, as a parameter
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Felix Oghină reports USB-C hubs whose HDMI socket gives the sound
driver an ELD of 2 channels of PCM and nothing else, while the chain
behind them (a TV and a sound bar on eARC) takes Dolby TrueHD, Dolby
Digital Plus and PCM in 8 channels (PR #29). The HDA HDMI codec limits
every stream to what the ELD declares, the most channels and the union
of the rates of all its descriptors (snd_hdmi_eld_update_pcm_info()),
so TrueHD (8 channels at 192 kHz) and Dolby Digital Plus (192 kHz)
cannot be opened, and decoded surround is mixed down to stereo. Whether
such data come from the converter or from the display behind it is not
known from the source.

The display parameter pcon_hd_audio (i915.pcon_hd_audio, xe.pcon_hd_audio;
off by default) gives such an ELD, in place of its descriptors:

- linear PCM in 8 channels, at the rates and sample sizes that the
  display data declare for PCM (at least 32, 44.1 and 48 kHz at 16
  bits, basic audio), so that the sample size that Kodi sends a display
  (16 bits where it declares fewer than 24, issue #23) is still the
  display's;
- Dolby Digital in 6 channels (CTA-861 code 2; 32 to 48 kHz, 640
  kbit/s), Dolby Digital Plus in 8 (code 10; 32 to 48 kHz) and Dolby
  TrueHD, as MAT, in 8 (code 12; 44.1 to 192 kHz), their
  format-dependent byte at zero;
- the speakers of 7.1 in its speaker allocation, since the HDA codec
  offers channel maps up to the speakers that it declares;
- a baseline length of what the descriptors take, as the specification
  and drm_eld_calc_baseline_block_size() count it.

DTS is not declared: Kodi passes through what its own settings say,
whatever the ELD says, and the display data would otherwise claim
something that nobody has checked.

Only where the port's DPCD says that a branch device of the HDMI type
is behind it, with an HDMI sink, on a single stream; only where the ELD
declares PCM in 2 channels at most and nothing else (or no descriptor,
basic audio, which is handled as stereo PCM in the first place, not a
skipped one). A DisplayPort monitor, an MST hub, a display that
declares more, and anything that is not an ELD of version 2 that fits
are left as they are, byte for byte. The kernel log says what the
parameter did on a connector, once for each change: the descriptors
given, or why it left them.

The codes are the ones of CTA-861 (2 Dolby Digital, 10 Dolby Digital
Plus, 12 MAT; 9 is One Bit Audio, 14 WMA Pro, 15 the extension code);
the first place holds PCM also where the ELD had no descriptor; the
baseline length counts 16 bytes, the monitor name and 3 bytes per
descriptor; and only what is behind a converter is changed, never a
DisplayPort monitor's ELD.

Not tried on hardware. Compiled with W=1 for i915 and xe: no warning.
Host test (35 checks), with the ELD read back by ALSA's rules and by
Kodi's own reading of it (AEPcmChannels.h before and after the sound
changes of 1.1): the ELDs that it changes and those it leaves; seven mutants
(TrueHD as code 9, a baseline 7 bytes too long, PCM not first where
there was no descriptor, no speakers, a widened ELD that declared more,
the declared rates dropped, DTS declared) are caught.

Based on PR #29 by Felix Oghină: the finding and the idea; the code is
written again.
---
 .../drm/i915/display/intel_display_params.c   |   5 +
 .../drm/i915/display/intel_display_params.h   |   1 +
 .../drm/i915/display/intel_display_types.h    |   2 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c       |  54 +++++++
 .../gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_pcon_audio.h   | 136 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 198 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_pcon_audio.h

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_params.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_params.c
index 6aa4b53..1d56a9c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_params.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_params.c
@@ -41,6 +41,11 @@ intel_display_param_named(dv_pcon, int, 0400,
 	"-1=the boards and converters where it was seen working, and others where user space asks for it [default], 0=off, 1=every converter "
 	"(experimental: a converter that does not carry the Dolby vendor InfoFrame shows no Dolby Vision, or no picture).");
 
+intel_display_param_named(pcon_hd_audio, bool, 0400,
+	"The audio of a display behind a DisplayPort to HDMI converter (an adapter, a USB-C hub) whose display data declare stereo PCM only: "
+	"give the sound driver PCM in 8 channels, Dolby Digital, Dolby Digital Plus and Dolby TrueHD, for a chain behind it that takes them "
+	"(default: false, the display data as they are; a format that the chain does not take plays nothing).");
+
 intel_display_param_named(hdmi_hdr_gmp, bool, 0400,
 	"HDR static metadata (the DRM InfoFrame) over the HDMI port of display version 9 "
 	"(Skylake to Comet Lake, Apollo Lake), in its gamut metadata DIP, so that the port offers "
